## P2 — UI improvements

### 12. Post detail content order
- Current: title → markdown body → hero image → tags → meta.
- Expected blog layout: title → meta → hero image → body → tags.
- **File:** `src/screens/PostDetailScreen.tsx`

### 13. Calendar "Close" button is a no-op
- `CalendarScreen` is a tab root; `navigation.goBack()` does nothing useful.
- **Fix:** Remove the Close chip, or replace with "Today" jump / month picker.

### 14. Feed hides search when empty
- Search/sort hidden when `blogs.length === 0` and no active filter — new installs see bare empty state.
- **Fix:** Always show search bar; only hide sort chips when truly irrelevant.

### 15. Markdown editor promise vs reality
- Label says "Markdown supported"; `MarkdownContent` only renders fenced code blocks — no bold, italic, headings, links.
- **Fix (pick one):**
  - Implement inline parsing in `renderInlineText` (headings, `**bold**`, `*italic*`, links), OR
  - Add `react-native-markdown-display` and remove custom parser, OR
  - Soften label to "Plain text + code blocks".

### 16. Inconsistent iconography
- Mix of emoji (🔍 👍 👎 👁️) and `@expo/vector-icons`.
- **Fix:** Replace emoji with MaterialIcons for visual consistency and accessibility.

### 17. OfflineBanner ignores theme and safe area
- Hardcoded `#EF4444`, `top: 0` — overlaps status bar on notched devices.
- **Fix:** Use `useSafeAreaInsets()`, theme `destructive` color, green tint for "Back online".

### 18. Tab bar accessibility
- `tabBarShowLabel: false` — screen readers get icon-only tabs.
- **Fix:** Enable labels or add `tabBarAccessibilityLabel` per tab.

### 19. PostCard image placement
- Feed cards show title + preview text before image; hero image usually leads for visual scanning.
- **Fix:** Move image above preview text (match detail screen after P2 #12).

### 20. Login screen polish
- Google button uses text "G" instead of official icon; unused styles (`tagline`, `disclaimer`).
- **Fix:** Use `MaterialCommunityIcons` `google` or SVG asset; remove dead styles.

### 21. Light theme contrast on primary buttons
- `light-neutral` primary is `#1f2937` (dark gray) — fine, but verify WCAG on muted text (`#6b7280` on white).

